# Base ignores, from Azathothas/TEMPLATE dotfiles (common + rust + os-editor),
# with the additions this project needs.
#
# ⛔ .gitignore only applies to files git is not ALREADY tracking. Adding a line
# does not untrack what is already in. Check with: git ls-files

# -- secrets. Never committed, no exceptions ---------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*
!.dev.vars.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.keystore
id_rsa
id_ed25519
credentials.json
service-account*.json
*.token
.*_token
.*-token

# -- scratch and temporary work ---------------------------------------------
.tmp/
tmp/
temp/
scratch/
.scratch/

# -- logs --------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
logs/

# experiments/results/ is EVIDENCE, and a log there is the evidence itself.
# The two rules above are unanchored. Measured on 2026-09-11, they excluded 83
# experiment logs of the reference corpus; measured on 2026-11-06, they had
# also hidden three result logs of sweep163. A citation into one of them
# resolves on one disk and not in a fresh clone, which is the defect
# podvm-gate exists to catch.
!experiments/results/**/*.log

# -- coverage and test output -----------------------------------------------
coverage/
.coverage
htmlcov/
test-results/
.nyc_output/

# -- agent and assistant local files ----------------------------------------
.claude/settings.local.json
CLAUDE.local.md
.aider*
.cursorignore

# -- Rust --------------------------------------------------------------------
# ⛔ ROOTED. A bare `target/` also matched source directories named `target`
# in the reference corpus, and it would match one in `vendor/` too.
/target/
# ⛔ AND THE INTERPOSER HAS ITS OWN. It is excluded from the workspace, so it
# builds into its own target directory, which the rooted rule above does not
# reach. Measured on 2026-09-08: 23 build artefacts were committed before this
# line existed.
/crates/podvm-interpose/target
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Cargo.lock IS committed: podvm ships a binary and the lock is what makes a
# build reproducible.

# -- experiment scratch ------------------------------------------------------
# ⛔ ONE RULE, NOT A LIST. Every experiment writes to `experiments/.<name>/`,
# and a per-directory list is a list somebody has to remember to extend.
# Measured on 2026-09-08: `100-interpose-symbols.sh` exports a rootfs into
# `experiments/.symbols/`, and about 1400 files of somebody else's distribution
# were committed because the list did not have that name in it yet.
# `experiments/results/` is tracked: it is the evidence.
experiments/.*/
verification/build/

# `references/` holds MANIFEST.tsv and README.md only. The captured trees left
# the live tree on 2026-11-06; each one is tracked in a GitHub issue, and the
# manifest keeps every citation into them checked. Do not capture a tree here
# again: docs/methodology/references.md, section Corpus.

# ⛔ Windows reserved device names. A shell that does not map `2>/dev/null`
# creates a real file called `nul`, which breaks `git stash`.
nul
CON
PRN
AUX
NUL
COM[1-9]
LPT[1-9]
CON.*
PRN.*
AUX.*
NUL.*
COM[1-9].*
LPT[1-9].*

# -- OS and editor noise -----------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*.lnk

__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# podvm-dev state: the background build log and its stamp.
.dev/
dist/

# ⭐ The CodeGraph index. It is one machine's SQLite database, 230 MiB on the
# tree it was built over, and `podvm-dev session` rebuilds it. The
# directory carries its own ignore file; this line keeps the directory itself
# out of `git status`, which is what an agent reads to decide the tree is clean.
#
# ⛔ ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH, so it matches this repository's own index
# and nothing else. Unanchored, the pattern also matched
# `references/Azathothas__bit-cli/tree/.codegraph/`, which is a TRACKED corpus
# file. Git does not untrack what it already tracks, so nothing was lost, but
# an ignore rule over evidence is a rule waiting to drop it.
/.codegraph/

# ⚠ The staged payload that `scripts/windows/run-in-base.sh` writes beside the
# checkout and removes on exit. A cancelled run leaves one behind.
.podvm-job.sh

# ⛔ `refactor/` is untracked working material, not the record. Its audit
# files cite scripts and experiments that no longer exist, and the record
# gate resolves citations in every tracked markdown file, so tracking this
# directory turns a green gate red (measured 2026-10-01: 1047 problems from
# this directory alone). Do not force-add it. Since 2026-11-06 it lives on the
# branch archive/podbox-worktree: docs/history/worktree-archive.md says how to
# read it.
/refactor/

# Agent scratch: the org watcher state, cloud-setup downloads, parallel worktrees.
.work/
.claude/worktrees/

# TODO/gate.md T-1684: the output of cargo fuzz.
/crates/podvm-interpose/fuzz/target/
/crates/podvm-interpose/fuzz/corpus/
/crates/podvm-interpose/fuzz/artifacts/
/crates/podvm-interpose/fuzz/coverage/
